This is a Neovim configuration built on LazyVim. It includes two custom plugins in dev/.

## Key Facts

- Entry point: init.lua → lua/config/lazy.lua (bootstraps lazy.nvim + LazyVim)
- Plugin specs live in lua/plugins/ (each file returns a lazy.nvim spec table)
- Custom plugins: dev/claudeide.nvim (MCP server) and dev/codechat.nvim (AI terminal driver)
- Leader key: , (comma)
- Lua style: 2-space indent, 120 column width (stylua.toml)
- Format with: stylua lua/
- nvim-lint is explicitly disabled
- kotlin_language_server is disabled; Treesitter fallback used for Kotlin symbols

## Writing Plugin Code

- Use vim.uv (not vim.loop) for async I/O — this config targets Neovim 0.10+
- Custom plugins load via event = "VeryLazy" plus explicit cmd/keys tables
- Both custom plugins depend on no external Lua libraries (pure Lua + Neovim APIs)
- codechat.nvim depends on folke/snacks.nvim for terminals and floating windows
- claudeide.nvim implements WebSocket + MCP protocol from scratch using vim.uv TCP

## Architecture: claudeide.nvim

Pure-Lua WebSocket MCP server (JSON-RPC 2.0, protocol version 2025-03-26):
- server/ — TCP listener, HTTP upgrade handshake, WebSocket frame codec
- mcp.lua + tools.lua — MCP tool dispatch (openFile, openDiff)
- diff.lua — Blocking side-by-side diff with accept/deny
- lockfile.lua — Discovery files at ~/.claude/ide/<port>.lock
- selection.lua — Broadcasts selection_changed notifications

## Architecture: codechat.nvim

Terminal driver for CLI coding agents:
- terminal.lua — Terminal lifecycle, bracketed paste injection
- ui.lua — Comment popup (Snacks float) before sending context
- config.lua — Agent registry (command, setup, login shell, fallbacks)

## Environment

- Node.js 22 via nvm (needed for ttadk/cl commands)
- ttadk CLI (internal tool) for wrapped agent access
- LazyVim extras: editor.outline, lang.java, lang.json, lang.kotlin, lang.markdown
